#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:27
msgid "Implementation Requirements / Goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:29
msgid ""
"The highest priority is to be as accurate as possible, according to the C "
"and IEEE 754 standards.  By default, we will aim to be correctly rounded for "
"`all rounding modes <https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/numeric/fenv/"
"FE_round>`_. The current rounding mode of the floating point environment is "
"used to perform computations and produce the final results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:34
msgid ""
"To test for correctness, we compare the outputs with other correctly rounded "
"multiple-precision math libraries such as the `GNU MPFR library <https://www."
"mpfr.org/>`_ or the `CORE-MATH library <https://core-math.gitlabpages.inria."
"fr/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:38
msgid ""
"Our next requirement is that the outputs are consistent across all "
"platforms. Notice that the consistency requirement will be satisfied "
"automatically if the implementation is correctly rounded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:42
msgid ""
"Our last requirement for the implementations is to have good and predicable "
"performance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:45
msgid ""
"The average performance should be comparable to other ``libc`` "
"implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:47
msgid "The worst case performance should be within 10X-20X of the average."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:48
msgid ""
"Platform-specific implementations or instructions could be added whenever it "
"makes sense and provides significant performance boost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../headers/math/index.rst:51
msgid ""
"For other use cases that have strict requirements on the code size, memory "
"footprint, or latency, such as embedded systems, we will aim to be as "
"accurate as possible within the memory or latency budgets, and consistent "
"across all platforms."
msgstr ""

